# LF in the working tree on every platform. A Windows clone with core.autocrlf
# checked out CRLF, and the front-matter and markdown parsers in the tests, the
# eval builder and docs/privacy/build.mjs are written for "\n" (the privacy build
# spun forever on "## Heading\r"). They now tolerate CRLF too; this keeps the
# checkout from producing it in the first place.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated diagram figures: byte-stable output from tools/render-mermaid.mjs.
# Without this, git line-ending normalisation rewrites them on every checkout
# and the "same input -> identical output" guarantee looks broken when it is not.
docs/report/figures/** -text
*.svg -text
